    [Doc][BugFix] Fix MiniMax-M3 deployment and request examples (#19980)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    Sync the complete documentation fixes from #19953 to main. The
    MiniMax-M3 guide contains missing shell variable definitions,
    inconsistent deployment instructions, and request examples that can fail
    when copied. Align the A3 PD introduction with its W8A8 examples, define
    and quote single-node weight/log paths, and explain container checks,
    multi-node verification, and `max-num-seqs` tuning.
    
    Fix the tool-call parser option and broken shell quoting in the tool
    request; align the SDK example with the documented service port and
    explain using the proxy address for PD. Clarify that omitting multimodal
    limits does not disable multimodal support. Consolidate pooling
    references, explain Master TTL units, link functional verification,
    remove an unrelated GLM warning, and add the Video-MME dataset source.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    No runtime changes. Documentation only; existing parallelism and serving
    parameter values are unchanged. Main-specific version wording is
    retained.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    - `codespell`, `typos`, and `markdownlint` hooks, `git diff --check`,
    and a full MkDocs build passed on main.
    - Compared every added/deleted line with #19953: the patches match. The
    resulting documents differ only in two pre-existing branch-specific
    lines; all code examples match the validated release PR.
    - #19953 validation covered Bash syntax and target/draft paths
    containing spaces, speculative JSON expansion, the corrected curl JSON,
    Unicode text-request JSON, SDK Python syntax, and internal link targets.
    No NPU services or live inference requests were started.
    - Attempted `bash format.sh ci`; it waited on the shared pre-commit
    directory lock and was stopped after 20 seconds. Focused checks passed.
    
    ### Checklist
    - [x] Reviewed shell quoting and empty-path boundary cases; examples
    checked with mock commands.
    - [x] Recorded focused documentation validation; no runtime source code
    changed.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/544f182d9f0c9bfe8bd7645525951d5e3692a542
    
